      "observation": "All six corrected idle captures and both retained static walk captures were visually inspected. Two wings, two dangling legs/feet, the narrow neck and long beak remain complete and in side profile in both directions. The downstroke tip now ends above the projected physical floor instead of crossing it. The body does not grow or shrink with wing height; head/feet landmarks remain stable after compensating for ordinary actor movement and mirror. The slight uniform lift of idle relative to the preserved glide/walk is acceptable for this flying subject; no further anchor change is recommended.",
      "limitations": [
        "The downstroke has about 1.01 screen pixels of framing clearance in this idle setup; the assertion tolerance remains 2 pixels and was not relaxed. This is verified on Hazel Street Subway, not every dynamic combat state.",
        "The common idle anchor moved from .735 to .745, raising all idle images by 3.629 screen pixels in this camera. The preserved walk stays unchanged, so a small vertical presentation offset remains at the transition.",
        "The retained walk has one frame [3]. Movement is not a newly generated multi-frame walk animation, and its historical beak contour differs slightly from the idle reconstruction.",
        "Only six idle pose captures and two static movement captures were manually inspected. The ninth preserved-selection capture was generated but not manually reviewed in this step.",
        "The authored idle timing and source-guided reconstruction do not certify original source timing, canonical measurements, hidden-side anatomy or one-to-one fidelity."
      ],
      "contact": "The flyer body offset and floating feet remain intentional. The lowest readable wing pixel is at screen y=592.638 and its framing fringe at y=592.993, above projected floor y=594 in both orientations. No apparent floor penetration remains in the downstroke captures.",
